        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Broadcasting and field archives shaped how Quebecois trad repertoire spread internationally.\n\nBest study habit: **Listen to regional recordings and compare with the anchor unit.**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "compared-with-quebec",
      "title": "Compared with Quebec",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Diaspora scenes remix anchor traditions with local dance floors, radio, and language communities. Compare accent and social context — not only tune titles."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "key-points",
      "title": "Key points",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "- Diaspora traditions carry anchor roots into new institutional settings.\n- Comparative listening prevents flattening regional specificity.\n- Festivals and archives link communities across borders."
        }
      ]
    },
